C. albicans
samples combining the yeast-specific databases with the
E. coli
database. This analysis revealed a considerable fraction of
E. coli
contamination in all samples although highest standards were followed for clean work (Fig.
5
B). The fraction of PSMs covering CUG codons is between 1.3 and 1.7% for
C. albicans
and between 2.0 and 3.2% for
M. acacia
. These fractions together with respective numbers of PSMs fit to the
E. coli
